From e0e620c90c1bdfb0c32cbb55bc71f7f247dccb7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:21:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban_move: refuse a move for ship custody;
 hermes-core-wt ship lands from every host

Why: on 2026-11-12, PR1187's owner (t_01a1cce501c36450), approved and CI-green, moved itself to
machine:hub because 'Final hermes-core-wt ship must run in genuine hub task custody'. It then sat
ready behind the hub's full local lane (6/7 busy) for 45+ minutes. That advice was stale. Since the
state ship gate judges moved runs and remote reviews from the Board's execution record, ship lands
from any machine: PR1318 landed from hermes-worker-3 the same hour. Card t_01a1cf350800e915
proposed a dispatcher ship lane. Its independent design review returned REPLAN: no tool can be the
marker's producer (the ship tooling never moves cards), a replicated marker cannot be authenticated,
and an over-cap slot must bypass five capacity gates. Removing the cause keeps the goal instead.

What: move_task, move_queued and move_reclaim refuse a reason that claims ship/landing custody
(reason_code ship_custody_portable) unless host_reason names a real host-only need. The refusal
says to run ship where the card runs. No dispatcher change.

Proof:
- Read-only replay over every board replica and local DB found 651 real moved events. The
  classifier matches 2: PR1187's, and the custody card's own diagnostic move, which host_reason
  admits. Real ship-adjacent non-custody reasons are negative test cases.
- The new file fails at HEAD (wiring absent).
- 13/13 mutants killed.
- 13 move/repin/placement files pass, 255 tests; 4 kanban_tools files pass, 111 tests.
---
